# Stage 3 training guardrails

## Do NOT start training unless the user explicitly asks

Never run `train.py` with a real budget (anything beyond `--smoke` or a
user-requested `--timesteps` probe) without the user saying to start training
in the current conversation.

Allowed without asking:
- `python stage3-go2-training/train.py --smoke`
- `make train-smoke` / `make train-bench` (200k probe)
- Reading logs, `diagnose.py`, exporting checkpoints, rendering videos

Requires explicit user approval:
- Background `nohup` training runs
- `--timesteps` >= 500_000 or default 15M budgets
- `make train-gpu` / full production runs

When the user approves training, prefer:
1. `--flat-bootstrap` until `diagnose.py` shows walking (>0.15 m/s, >1.5 m/10s)
2. `--rollout-workers 0` (threaded MuJoCo — default)
3. Short probe first (`--timesteps 200000`), then diagnose, then longer budget
4. New `--run-name` after any reward-weight change — never `--resume` across them

See `docs/TRAINING-SPEED.md` and `.claude/skills/train/SKILL.md`.
